  "reference_solution": "WITH daily AS (SELECT day,SUM(COALESCE(amount,0)) AS amount FROM daily_activity GROUP BY day), spine AS (SELECT c.day,COALESCE(d.amount,0) AS daily_amount FROM calendar c LEFT JOIN daily d USING(day)) SELECT day,daily_amount,SUM(daily_amount) OVER(ORDER BY day ROWS BETWEEN 6 PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW) AS rolling_7d_amount FROM spine",
  "solution_explanation": "Aggregate to daily grain and join to the contiguous date spine before the window. A seven-row frame then equals seven reporting calendar days.",
  "hints": [
    "The calendar defines output population and elapsed dates.",
    "Multiple rows for a date must become one before a row-based frame.",
    "Fill missing days on the spine, then specify the frame explicitly."
  ],
  "senior_review": "A seven-row frame is only a seven-day frame after validating a contiguous unique calendar. Clarify reporting-history limits.",
